    passage: 'Football is the most popular sport in our school. Almost every boy plays it during lunch break, and many girls enjoy it as well. Our school team has twenty-four players, and we practise three times a week on the grass field behind the library. I joined the team two years ago because I wanted to make more friends and improve my fitness. At first, I was not very good at passing the ball or controlling it with my feet. However, my coach, Mr Zhang, taught me how to position myself, how to communicate with my teammates, and how to stay calm under pressure. We also do a lot of physical training, such as running laps and stretching, to keep our bodies strong. Last month, we played against a team from another school in the city. It was a tough game, but we scored two goals in the last ten minutes and won 3-2. The whole team cheered and hugged each other on the field. Football has taught me the importance of teamwork, discipline, and never giving up. I believe that playing football has made me a better student and a stronger person.',
