    passage: 'Last October, my parents took me to Beijing for a five-day trip. It was my first time visiting the capital, and I was extremely excited. On the first day, we went to the Palace Museum, also known as the Forbidden City. The buildings were painted in red and gold, and the roofs were decorated with little animals. I could not believe how huge the place was. On the second day, we climbed up the Jingshan Hill, and from the top we could see the whole Forbidden City stretching out below us. The view was breathtaking. On the third day, we visited the Temple of Heaven, where emperors used to pray for good harvests. I liked the round Hall of Prayer for Good Harvests the most because of its unique shape. We also walked around Tiananmen Square at night, and the lights made the square look very grand. Of course, we tried many famous Beijing dishes, such as Peking duck and jianbing for breakfast. I bought a small panda toy for my younger sister as a souvenir. Beijing is a city full of history and modern life, and I would love to visit it again soon.',
