    title: 'Using Computers Wisely',
    passage: 'Computers have become an important part of our daily life. In my family, we use computers for school, work, and fun. I usually use my laptop to do homework, search for information, and watch short videos in my free time. Last month, my teacher asked us to write a report about animals in danger. Instead of reading paper books, I searched online and found many useful articles in just ten minutes. I saved the information and organised it into a clear document. My teacher was surprised by how much I had written, and she gave me an A for the report. However, my parents worry that I spend too much time in front of the screen. We made a rule together: I can use the computer for only one hour on weekdays and two hours on weekends. I also have to stop using it one hour before bedtime so that I can sleep well. I think computers are very useful tools, but they should not replace outdoor activities. Reading on a screen is good, but reading a real book under a tree is much more enjoyable. Balance is the key to using technology wisely.',
