    serial: 14,
    category: '环境',
    title: 'The Problem of Plastic',
    passage: 'Plastic is everywhere in our modern life. We use plastic bags, plastic bottles, plastic straws, and plastic boxes every single day. However, plastic is also one of the biggest causes of pollution on our planet. Most plastic items take hundreds of years to break down, and many end up in the ocean. Sea animals such as turtles and dolphins often mistake plastic bags for food and eat them by accident. Sadly, this can make them very sick or even kill them. Scientists have found plastic inside the bodies of whales and seabirds on remote islands. To solve this problem, many countries have started to ban single-use plastic bags. In China, for example, most supermarkets no longer give out free plastic bags. People are encouraged to bring their own cloth bags when they go shopping. My family has used reusable cloth bags for two years, and we also bring our own water bottles to school. Small changes like these can really help reduce plastic pollution. Students can also take part by picking up plastic waste in parks or joining beach clean-ups. If everyone does a little, the world will become a much cleaner and safer place for animals and for us.',
