    category: '健康',
    title: 'Breakfast Is Important',
    passage: 'Do you always eat breakfast before going to school? Many teenagers skip breakfast because they are in a hurry or they are not hungry in the morning. However, doctors strongly advise us to have a good breakfast every day. A healthy breakfast gives us the energy we need to think and learn in class. Studies show that students who eat breakfast perform better in maths, reading, and sports than those who do not. A balanced breakfast should include some protein, such as eggs or milk, some carbohydrates like bread or porridge, and a piece of fruit for vitamins. I usually have a boiled egg, a bowl of oatmeal, and an apple before I leave home. Since I started eating breakfast every day, I have felt less tired in the morning and I can pay more attention to my teachers. My younger sister, on the other hand, often skips breakfast, and she always feels dizzy by ten o\'clock. Now my mother prepares breakfast for the whole family at seven o\'clock, and we eat together before school. It has become one of the best moments of our day, and we all feel closer as a family.',
