    passage: 'Swimming is my favourite summer sport. When the weather gets very hot, I usually go to the city swimming pool with my friends. I have been learning to swim since I was six years old, and I can now swim three different styles: freestyle, breaststroke, and backstroke. Freestyle is the fastest, but breaststroke is the easiest for long distances. My coach, Mr Wang, always reminds us about safety. He says we should never swim alone in deep water, and we should always warm up before getting into the pool. Last summer, I took part in a city-wide swimming competition. I was very nervous before the race, but I tried to stay calm and focus on my breathing. I swam the one hundred metre freestyle and finished second in my age group. Even though I did not win first place, I felt very proud because I had improved a lot compared with last year. My parents came to watch me, and they cheered loudly from the stands. After the race, my mother bought me a big ice cream to celebrate. Swimming is not only fun but also great exercise, because it uses almost every muscle in the body. I hope to keep swimming for many more years.',
