    category: '健康',
    title: 'Why We Need Sleep',
    passage: 'Sleep is one of the most important things we need to stay healthy, but many teenagers do not get enough of it. Experts say that teenagers should sleep at least eight to ten hours every night. When we sleep, our body repairs muscles, stores memories, and removes waste from the brain. Without enough sleep, we feel tired, find it hard to concentrate, and may even get sick more easily. Last year, I had a bad habit of staying up late to watch videos on my phone. After a few weeks, I could not pay attention in class, and my grades dropped. My parents and doctor warned me that lack of sleep was harming my health. I decided to change. I started going to bed at ten o\'clock every night and keeping my phone in another room after nine. Within two weeks, I felt much better. I had more energy in the morning, and my marks slowly improved. Now I keep a regular sleep routine: I brush my teeth, read a book for twenty minutes, and then go to sleep. Good sleep helps me study better, play sports better, and feel happier during the day. If you want to do well at school and stay healthy, the simplest answer is often a good night\'s sleep. Remember, sleep is not a waste of time; it is a gift you give to your future self.',
