    category: '科学',
    title: 'Our Solar System',
    passage: 'Our solar system is a family of objects that move around the Sun. It includes one star, the Sun, and eight planets, together with many moons, dwarf planets, asteroids, and comets. The Sun is at the centre, and it is so large that more than one million Earths could fit inside it. The Sun\'s gravity keeps the planets in their orbits, just as a string keeps a ball moving in a circle. From the closest to the Sun, the eight planets are Mercury, Venus, Earth, Mars, Jupiter, Saturn, Uranus, and Neptune. Mercury is the smallest and hottest during the day, while Jupiter is the largest, with a great red spot that is actually a giant storm. Earth is the only planet known to have life, because it has liquid water and a suitable atmosphere. Saturn is famous for its beautiful rings, which are made of ice and rock. Beyond Neptune lies Pluto, which was once called the ninth planet but is now known as a dwarf planet. Scientists continue to explore our solar system using powerful telescopes and space probes. They hope to find new information about how the planets formed and whether life exists anywhere else in the universe. Our solar system is just a tiny part of the huge Milky Way galaxy, which itself is only one of billions of galaxies in space.',
