    title: 'Our Basketball Team',
    passage: 'Basketball is one of the most popular sports in our school. Our school team, the Tigers, has twenty players who train together four times a week. We usually meet after class on the outdoor court next to the gym. Our coach, Ms Li, is a former national player, and she knows the game very well. She teaches us not only how to dribble, pass, and shoot, but also how to think quickly and trust our teammates. Every practice begins with a warm-up of running and stretching, and ends with a short team meeting where we discuss what we did well and what we need to improve. Last month, we took part in a city youth tournament. In the final game, we were behind by six points with only three minutes left. Nobody gave up. Our captain, Jack, scored two quick baskets, and our point guard, Tom, made an excellent three-point shot. With ten seconds remaining, I caught a long pass and made a lay-up to win the game by one point. The crowd went wild, and our whole team hugged each other on the court. We lifted the trophy together and shouted our team slogan. That night, I realised that basketball is not just about scoring points; it is about working together and never giving up. I will remember this moment for the rest of my life.',
