    title: 'Collecting Stamps',
    passage: 'My grandfather has been collecting stamps since he was a teenager. He has albums full of stamps from almost every country in the world. Some of them are more than one hundred years old. When I was small, I used to look at his albums with wide eyes, fascinated by the bright colours and strange pictures. Last year, my grandfather gave me my first album and a few old stamps to start my own collection. Since then, I have learned a lot about the hobby. Each stamp tells a small story about its country. Some show famous leaders, while others show rare animals, beautiful buildings, or important historical events. Stamp collecting, also known as philately, teaches us geography, history, and art at the same time. My favourite part is finding stamps from places I have never heard of before, and then searching online to learn about those countries. The most expensive stamp in my grandfather\'s collection is a small red stamp from China, worth more than five hundred thousand yuan. Of course, my collection is much smaller and less valuable, but I enjoy it just as much. Last weekend, my grandfather took me to a stamp fair in the city centre. I traded a few modern stamps with a collector and got a beautiful Japanese stamp in return. I am proud of my collection, and I hope to pass it on to my own grandchildren one day.',
