    title: 'A Train Journey',
    passage: 'Last summer, my family and I took a long train journey from our city to Chengdu. Although it took about twelve hours, I enjoyed every minute of it. We bought hard sleeper tickets, so we had small beds stacked three high in a small cabin. At first, I thought the train would be boring, but it turned out to be one of the most interesting trips I have ever taken. The scenery outside the window changed constantly. First, we passed busy cities with tall buildings, then wide green fields, then tall mountains with rivers running through them. As we moved further west, I could see farmers working in rice paddies and children waving at the train. In the dining car, we had hot noodles and tea, and the waiter told us funny stories about his travels. At night, the train rocked gently and the wheels made a soft "click-clack" sound that quickly put me to sleep. When I woke up the next morning, we were already in Sichuan Province. Outside the window, I saw pandas painted on the walls of small villages. Travelling by train is slower than flying, but it lets you see the country up close. You can watch the landscape change from cities to villages, from rivers to mountains. I would love to take another train journey soon, perhaps across northern China to see the grasslands.',
