    title: 'Healthy Eating at School',
    passage: 'Healthy eating is very important for students. Every morning, I try to have a balanced breakfast before I leave home. I usually eat an egg, a piece of whole wheat bread, a glass of milk, and a small bowl of fruit. This gives me the energy I need to pay attention in class until lunchtime. At school, I always buy a hot lunch from the canteen instead of eating chips or sweets from the snack bar. The lunch usually includes rice, vegetables, and some kind of meat or fish for protein. I also drink water during the day rather than sugary drinks. My science teacher once told us that the brain needs good food to work well, just like a car needs the right fuel. After school, I try to avoid eating too many biscuits or chocolate before dinner, even though they taste very nice. On weekends, my mother helps me prepare simple meals, and we sometimes cook together. Since I started following this habit, I have felt stronger and found it easier to focus on my studies. Eating well is not always easy, but it really helps both my body and my mind.',
