    passage: 'I picked up photography as a hobby two years ago, when my uncle gave me his old digital camera. At first, I only took pictures of my dog and the trees in our garden. Soon, I began to notice small things around me that other people usually miss, such as a leaf covered with dew, or a cat sleeping on a warm wall. My favourite subject is nature, especially flowers and insects, because their colours change with the light. Every Saturday morning, I take a walk in the nearby park with my camera in my bag. I try to use natural light instead of the flash, and I always look for a simple background to make the subject stand out. After taking photos, I spend time on the computer editing them carefully. I never change the colours too much, because I want my pictures to look real. Last year, three of my photos were shown in our school art exhibition, and my teacher said they had a quiet beauty. Now I share my best photos on a small online gallery, and I receive kind comments from people in different countries. Photography has taught me to slow down and look closely at the world.',
