    category: '历史',
    title: 'The Ancient Pyramids of Egypt',
    passage: 'The pyramids of Egypt are among the most amazing buildings in human history. They were built more than four thousand years ago, during the time of the ancient pharaohs. The largest of them all is the Great Pyramid of Giza, which was constructed for the pharaoh Khufu. It stands about one hundred and forty metres tall and is made of more than two million huge stone blocks. Each block weighs several tons, yet the stones fit together so perfectly that not even a knife can slide between them. No one knows exactly how the workers moved such heavy stones without modern machines, but many historians believe they used ramps, levers, and thousands of skilled workers. Inside the pyramids, there are narrow passages that lead to secret rooms where the kings were buried. The walls of these rooms were decorated with colourful paintings and old writings called hieroglyphs. Although most of the tombs have been opened long ago, scientists are still finding new things inside and around the pyramids. Today, the pyramids are visited by millions of tourists every year. They have become a powerful symbol of ancient Egypt and a reminder of how clever and hardworking people were, even thousands of years ago.',
