    title: 'A Family Trip to Hainan',
    passage: 'Last October, my family took a seven-day holiday in Hainan, the southernmost island of China. We flew from Beijing to Haikou, the capital city, and the flight took about four hours. When we stepped out of the airport, we were greeted by warm, humid air and bright sunshine, even though it was already autumn. Our hotel was right next to the beach, so we could hear the waves from our room at night. On the first day, we went swimming in the sea. The water was clear and not too cold, and we saw small colourful fish swimming near our feet. The next day, we visited a tropical forest park where there were hundreds of coconut trees, strange birds, and butterflies as big as my hand. My father drove us around the island for three days, and we stopped at different beaches, fishing villages, and fruit farms. We tried fresh mangoes, pineapples, and the famous Hainan coconut rice. One evening, we watched a wonderful performance of traditional Li and Miao dancing on the beach. The dancers wore bright silver clothes and smiled as they moved. By the end of the trip, my skin was a little darker, my bag was full of seashells, and my heart was full of happy memories. I hope to return to Hainan again next summer.',
