    category: '环境',
    title: 'Bees in Danger',
    passage: 'Bees are small insects, but they play one of the most important roles in nature. As they fly from flower to flower collecting nectar, they carry pollen on their bodies and help plants produce seeds and fruit. About one third of the food we eat, including apples, strawberries, almonds, and many vegetables, depends on bees for pollination. Without bees, our meals would be much poorer and our world would look very different. Sadly, bee populations around the world are getting smaller every year. Scientists have found several reasons for this. Pesticides used on farms can poison bees and make them unable to find their way home. Air pollution, climate change, and the loss of wild flowers also harm them. Diseases spread quickly through crowded bee colonies, and many beekeepers have lost almost all of their hives in recent years. People are now taking action to help bees. Some farmers are growing wild flowers along the edges of their fields. Cities are planting more bee-friendly gardens on rooftops and in parks. Even at home, we can help by leaving small dishes of clean water in our gardens and by not using harmful chemicals. Protecting bees means protecting the food we eat and the planet we live on.',
