    category: '科技',
    title: 'Using Tablets for Learning',
    passage: 'In our school, every student from Grade 5 onwards is given a tablet to help with their studies. At first, many parents were worried that we would only use the tablets to play games. However, our teachers showed us how to use them well, and now I find my tablet is one of the most useful tools I have. In class, my teacher sends digital notes and short videos to our tablets so we can follow the lesson more easily. If I do not understand something, I can watch the video again at home, as many times as I need. For homework, I can solve maths problems by tapping the screen, and the tablet checks my answers immediately. I also use my tablet to read e-books, learn new English words, and practice writing. When I am working on a group project, my friends and I share files quickly through the cloud, even when we are at home in different places. Of course, we are taught to use the tablets sensibly. We must put them away during meals, and we are not allowed to use them after 9 p.m. I think technology does not replace teachers, but it certainly makes learning more interesting and more personal for me.',
