    title: 'Learning to Swim',
    passage: 'Last summer, my parents decided that I should learn to swim. I was both excited and a little nervous, because I had never put my face in deep water before. On the first day at the swimming pool, my coach, Mr Wang, was very patient with me. He taught me how to breathe slowly, how to float on my back, and how to kick my legs in the water. At first, I swallowed a lot of water and felt quite tired after only ten minutes. But my coach always encouraged me and said that everyone feels clumsy at the beginning. After two weeks of practice, I could float by myself and swim a short distance using the freestyle stroke. Then I learned how to turn my head to the side to breathe without stopping. Slowly, my fear of water disappeared, and I started to enjoy the feeling of gliding through the cool, blue water. By the end of the summer, I could swim one full length of the pool without stopping. I was so proud of myself that I told all my classmates about it. Now I swim at least once a week, both for exercise and for fun. Learning to swim has given me confidence, and I hope to join the school swim team next year.',
