    category: '健康',
    title: 'Why Sleep Matters',
    passage: 'Most teenagers need about eight to ten hours of sleep every night, but studies show that many students in China sleep much less than this. There are several reasons why sleep is so important. First, while we sleep, our brains sort and store everything we have learned during the day. Without enough rest, it is much harder to remember new words, formulae, or historical events. Second, sleep helps our bodies grow and repair themselves. Growth hormones are mainly released at night, which is why babies and young people need more sleep than adults. Third, a good night\'s sleep keeps our mood stable. Students who sleep poorly often feel anxious, tired, and less able to focus on their lessons. Sleep also strengthens our immune system, so people who sleep well usually get sick less often. To improve sleep, experts suggest going to bed and waking up at the same time every day, even on weekends. They also advise keeping phones and computers out of the bedroom, because the blue light from screens tricks the brain into thinking it is still daytime. Avoiding heavy meals and energetic exercise close to bedtime is also helpful. Making sleep a priority is one of the simplest ways to become a healthier and better student.',
