    title: 'The World of 3D Printing',
    passage: '3D printing is one of the most exciting technologies of the twenty-first century. Unlike a normal printer that puts ink on paper, a 3D printer builds real objects layer by layer, using materials such as plastic, metal, or even chocolate. First, a person designs a model on a computer, then the printer follows the design and prints the object from the bottom up. It can take a few hours or even a whole day to finish, depending on the size and complexity of the object. Today, 3D printing is used in many fields. Doctors use it to make custom-made bones and teeth for patients. Engineers use it to create models of new machines before building the real ones. Architects print small versions of buildings to show their ideas to clients. In space, scientists have even used 3D printers on the International Space Station to make tools that would be hard to send from earth. In education, students like us can design our own toys, models, or simple machine parts and print them in our school\'s technology lab. Of course, 3D printing also raises some questions. People worry that it could be used to copy expensive products without permission. Still, most experts believe 3D printing will continue to change the way we design, learn, and live.',
