    title: 'Football: My Favourite Sport',
    passage: 'Football, also known as soccer in some countries, is my favourite sport in the world. I started playing it when I was seven years old, after my father took me to watch a match at the city stadium. The roar of the crowd and the speed of the players made my heart beat fast, and I decided right then that I wanted to learn the game. Since then, football has been a big part of my life. I play with my friends on a small pitch near my home almost every weekend, and I also train twice a week with my school team. In a match, there are eleven players on each side, and the aim is simple: score more goals than the other team. Only the goalkeeper can use his hands, while the other players must control the ball with their feet, chest, or head. Football teaches me important lessons, such as teamwork, fair play, and never giving up. I love the feeling of passing the ball perfectly to a teammate, or of scoring a goal after a long, hard game. Even when we lose, I learn something new and try to do better next time. My dream is to one day play for my country, but for now, I am happy to be part of a team I truly love.',
